{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-4059","published":"2026-09-25T01:27:51Z","modified":"2026-09-25T01:45:11.312475147Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-77159"],"summary":"libvirt security update","details":"Libvirt is a C toolkit to interact with the virtualization capabilities of recent versions of Linux (and other OSes). The main package includes the libvirtd server exporting the virtualization support.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA symlink-following flaw was found in libvirt&apos;s qemuTPMEmulatorPrepareHost() function. The function uses a path-based chown() on the swtpm logfile without checking for symbolic links. A local attacker with access to the swtpm account can replace the logfile with a symlink, causing libvirtd (running as root) to transfer ownership of an arbitrary file to the swtpm user.(CVE-2026-77159)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libvirt","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/libvirt&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["libvirt-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-admin-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-bash-completion-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-client-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-config-network-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-config-nwfilter-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-interface-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-network-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-nodedev-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-nwfilter-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-qemu-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-secret-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-core-6.2.0-30.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-st